(1) INFO ABOUT UTILITY
=======================================================================================================

This is the catpkg-cli installation assistant for installing the primary packages
(the catpkg package manager itself is not required).

It is an executable CAST archive containing the required binary files, packages,
package information, and cast-cli. In the case of catstrap, cast-cli is executable
and performs the role of the installer.

catstrap can be used on an empty minimal system to pre-install the packages required
for the system to operate. It initializes the catstrap database and serves as the
primary package manager during the initial installation process.


Permissions:

`--install`
    Root privileges required.

`--remove`
    Root privileges required.

`--update`
    Root privileges required.

`--packages`
    Default user permissions.

`--list`
    Default user permissions.


# (2) COMMANDS
=======================================================================================================

## (2.1) INSTALL
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install`

Install or update all packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install <package_name>`

Install or update a package provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install catpkg`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install <package_name_1> <package_name_2> <package_name_N>`

Install or update several packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --install filesystem catstrap-bin catstraplib catpkg`

Before installation, catstrap-catpkg displays information about the package
and asks for confirmation.

The command requires root privileges.

## (2.2) UPDATE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update`

Update all packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update <package_name>`

Update a package provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update catpkg`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update <package_name_1> <package_name_2> <package_name_N>`

Update several packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --update filesystem catstrap-bin catstraplib catpkg`

Before updating, catstrap-catpkg displays information about the package
and asks for confirmation.

The command requires root privileges.


## (2.3) REMOVE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove`

Remove all packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove <package_name>`

Remove a package provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove catpkg`

OR

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove <package_name_1> <package_name_2> <package_name_N>`

Remove several packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --remove filesystem catstrap-bin catstraplib catpkg`

Before removal, catstrap-catpkg displays information about the package
and asks for confirmation.

The command requires root privileges.


## (2.4) PACKAGES
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Usage:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --packages`

Outputs a list of packages provided by `catstrap-catpkg`, including their names,
to the console.

Example:

`sudo catstrap-catpkg-* --packages`


